  <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 italic mb-8">
    *Note: Many networks (including Tesla, bp pulse, and IONITY Passport) offer monthly subscription tiers costing £8.99 to £11.99 per month that discount per-kWh rates by 15% to 25%. If you rapid-charge more than twice a month, these subscriptions pay for themselves immediately.
  </p>

  <!-- Section 3 -->
  <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">
    3. The Financial Reality: Is Public Rapid Charging More Expensive Than Petrol?
  </h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Many prospective EV motorists are stunned to discover that <strong>on a pure pence-per-mile basis, motorway rapid charging frequently costs MORE than driving a petrol car</strong>. Let us examine the exact mathematical proof using current UK fuel prices:
  </p>

  <div class="my-6 p-6 bg-gray-50 border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-3xl not-prose font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-900 space-y-3">
    <div>
      <strong class="text-red-700">Petrol Car Formula (45 UK Imperial MPG @ £1.45/Litre):</strong><br/>
      1 Imperial Gallon = 4.54609 Litres. Gallon price = £1.45 × 4.54609 = <strong>£6.59</strong>.<br/>
      Cost Per Mile = £6.59 ÷ 45 MPG = <strong class="text-red-800">£0.146 (14.6p per mile)</strong>.
    </div>
    <div class="pt-2 border-t border-gray-200">
      <strong class="text-amber-800">Motorway Rapid EV (InstaVolt @ 87p/kWh @ 3.5 mi/kWh):</strong><br/>
      Cost Per Mile = £0.87 ÷ 3.5 miles = <strong class="text-amber-900">£0.248 (24.8p per mile)</strong>.
    </div>
    <div class="pt-2 border-t border-gray-200">
      <strong class="text-emerald-700">Verdict:</strong><br/>
      Driving 100 motorway miles on InstaVolt costs <strong>£24.80</strong> in electricity. Driving the same 100 miles in a 45 MPG petrol car costs <strong>£14.60</strong> in fuel—meaning ultra-rapid charging is <strong class="text-red-700">70% more expensive than petrol per mile!</strong>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    This financial dynamic is why drivers without home charging who rely 100% on motorway chargers often struggle to see operational fuel savings. However, this comparison only tells half the story.
  </p>

  <!-- Section 4 -->
  <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">
    4. The 80/20 Rule: How Real UK EV Drivers Still Save £1,100+ Every Year
  </h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Real-world telematics show that typical British motorists do not charge exclusively at motorway rapid chargers. Over <strong>80% of routine vehicle charging occurs at home overnight</strong>, where tariffs are radically cheaper. As detailed in our comprehensive guide comparing <a href="/blog/uk-ev-charging-cost-octopus-go-vs-price-cap" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">UK EV Charging Costs: Octopus Go vs Ofgem Price Cap</a> (see our full <a href="/blog/ev-charging-cost-uk-2026" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">UK EV Home Charging Guide</a>), smart energy tariffs charge as little as <strong>7.0p per kWh</strong> between 11:30 PM and 5:30 AM.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    Consider an average UK motorist covering <strong>10,000 miles per year</strong> who follows the standard <strong>80/20 charging split</strong> (8,000 miles charged at home, 2,000 miles charged on motorway rapid networks):
  </p>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto my-8 bg-white rounded-2xl border-2 border-gray-200 not-prose shadow-sm">
    <table class="w-full text-xs text-left border-collapse">
      <thead class="bg-gray-100 text-gray-950 font-black uppercase text-[11px] border-b border-gray-200">
        <tr>
          <th class="p-3.5">Fueling &amp; Charging Strategy</th>
          <th class="p-3.5">Average Cost Per Mile</th>
          <th class="p-3.5">10,000-Mile Annual Spend</th>
          <th class="p-3.5 text-emerald-800">Annual Net Pocket Savings</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 text-gray-700 font-medium">
        <tr class="bg-emerald-50/70 font-semibold">
          <td class="p-3.5 font-black text-emerald-950">80% Home (Octopus 7p) + 20% Rapid (Tesla 59p)</td>
          <td class="p-3.5 font-black text-emerald-700">4.97p / mile</td>
          <td class="p-3.5 font-black text-emerald-900">£497.00 / year</td>
          <td class="p-3.5 font-black text-emerald-800">+£1,151 Saved vs Petrol</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-gray-950">80% Home (Ofgem 24.5p) + 20% Rapid (InstaVolt 87p)</td>
          <td class="p-3.5">10.56p / mile</td>
          <td class="p-3.5">£1,056.00 / year</td>
          <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-emerald-700">+£592 Saved vs Petrol</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="bg-red-50/50">
          <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-950">100% Public Rapid Only (Avg 79p/kWh)</td>
          <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-800">22.57p / mile</td>
          <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-900">£2,257.00 / year</td>
          <td class="p-3.5 text-red-800">-£609 Loss vs Petrol</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-t-2 border-gray-200">
          <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-gray-950">45 MPG Petrol Car Baseline (£1.45 / Litre)</td>
          <td class="p-3.5">16.48p / mile</td>
          <td class="p-3.5">£1,648.00 / year</td>
          <td class="p-3.5 text-gray-500">Baseline Forecourt Burn</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    By anchoring your routine charging to an off-peak home tariff and using Tesla Superchargers or grocery hub destination chargers for long-distance trips, your blended running cost remains under <strong>5.0p per mile</strong>—saving more than <strong>£1,150 every single year on fuel alone</strong>. In our dedicated research paper on <a href="/blog/ev-charging-cost-vs-petrol-2026" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">EV Charging Cost vs Petrol (Global Telemetry &amp; Break-Even Math)</a>, we demonstrate that when combined with reduced mechanical servicing expenses and zero engine oil requirements, total break-even is achieved within 2.5 to 3 years.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-12 mb-6 tracking-tight">
    Frequently Asked Questions (UK Public Charging Prices)
  </h2>

  <div class="space-y-4 my-6 not-prose">
    <details class="group bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden cursor-pointer shadow-xs hover:border-emerald-400 transition-all" open>
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center text-sm font-black text-gray-950">
        <span>Which public EV charging network is the cheapest in the UK?</span>
        <span class="text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform"><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></span>
      </summary>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-3 font-medium">
