      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="group bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden cursor-pointer shadow-xs hover:border-emerald-400 transition-all">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center text-sm font-black text-gray-950">
        <span>Can any non-Tesla electric car use UK Tesla Superchargers?</span>
        <span class="text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform"><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></span>
      </summary>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-3 font-medium">
        Yes, over 40% of Tesla Supercharger locations across the UK are now officially open to all electric vehicles with a standard CCS2 charging port. You simply download the Tesla smartphone app, add your payment card, and select 'Charge Non-Tesla'.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="group bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden cursor-pointer shadow-xs hover:border-emerald-400 transition-all">
      <summary class="flex justify-between items-center text-sm font-black text-gray-950">
        <span>Is public rapid charging in the UK more expensive than petrol?</span>
        <span class="text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform"><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i></span>
      </summary>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-3 font-medium">
        Yes, if evaluated purely on motorway ultra-rapid rates (79p to 92p per kWh), an EV costs 22p to 26p per mile compared to 14.6p per mile for a 45 MPG petrol car. However, when combined with 80% home charging (7p/kWh on smart tariffs), the overall average drops to under 5.0p per mile, preserving large savings.
      </p>
